Mandatory Syntax Rules

• Declare the data type first. Every variable needs a type before its name (e.g., int age = 25;).
• Allowed characters. Names can only contain letters, digits, underscores (_), and dollar signs ($).
• Starting character. Names must start with a letter, _, or $—never a digit (1num is invalid).
• No spaces. Variable names cannot contain blank spaces (my age is invalid).
• No reserved keywords. You cannot use Java keywords like int, class, public, or void as variable names.
• Case-sensitive. age and Age are treated as two completely different variables.

Standard Naming Conventions (Best Practices)

• Use camelCase. Start with a lowercase letter and capitalize subsequent words (e.g., studentName, totalAmount).
• Constants in UPPER_CASE. Use all caps with underscores for final constant variables (e.g., final int MAX_SPEED = 120;).
